I have several small suggestions.

1.  Handling of mail.  I think it would be nice to have a mail option,
    so one can toggle mail off if s/he doesn't want to be disturbed
    in the middle of a game.
    Additionally, I think reading a scroll of mail should take 0 turns.
    There are times when suddenly getting an extra scroll of mail pushes you
    over your weight limit, forcing you to use up game time to get
    rid of something.  Mail shouldn't affect the play of the game.
    You could be running from monsters, and suddenly have to take time
    to drop the mail scroll or read it.  Another solution would be
    to have the scroll of mail WEIGH 0, but this is slightly inferior
    to my other solution since there is also the 52(?) pack-slot
    limit, and mail occupying space when you're near THAT limit may
    conceivably cause problems.

2.  It would be nice to have your discoveries listed in the same order
    as you have chosen for your inventory.

3.  The "O" command followed by return, when it's supposed to list your
    option settings, is a little screwy...only lists some of my packorder,
    plus leaves out a lot of stuff.  (All this is patchlevel 8, on a UNIX
    4.3 BSD system.)

4.  Scoring per "name" rather than per uid should take into account BOTH
    character name AND uid, to take care of the situation when people
    have the same character name as someone else.  It would be cumbersome
    and unaesthetic to list the character name and uid (or username) in
    the high-scores list, but both should be checked in determining what
    goes on the list. 


Admittedly minor stuff.  Altogether a great game!
